-- title:
--   Evaluated Slice Phase Five Paper Reindex To Raw Defect
-- statement:
--   **The swapped phase-five defect reindexes to the raw scalar stability defect.**
--
--   Let the LIDT parameters, field model, symmetric strategy, slice family, polynomial-valued map $G$, and identification $G(x)=(\mathrm{family.meas}\,x).\mathrm{toSubMeas}$ be as above. On an evaluated-slice question $Q=((u,x),(v,y))$, `evaluatedSlicePhaseFivePaperSwappedDefect` is the phase-five missing-mass expression after exchanging the two right-register point effects, so its right factor is $A_2(Q,b)A_1(Q,a)$ rather than $A_1(Q,a)A_2(Q,b)$. Then its uniform average over evaluated-slice questions is exactly the uniform field average of the raw two-sided scalar $G$-commutativity defect:
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb{E}_{Q\sim\mathrm{Unif}(\mathcal Q)}
--   \bigl[\mathrm{evaluatedSlicePhaseFivePaperSwappedDefect}(Q)\bigr]
--   =\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathrm{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q)}
--   \bigl[\mathrm{gCommStabilityTwoRawScalarDefect}(x)\bigr].
--   $$
--
--   The result is the exact finite reindexing step that connects the paper-faithful evaluated-slice calculation to the raw scalar stability quantity used by `evaluatedSlice_scalar_chain_bound`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.evaluatedSlice_phaseFivePaper_reindex_to_raw_defect`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
